3. Progressive disclosure and encapsulation (hard rule)
The user sees the minimum needed to decide or act. Everything else stays one tap away or hidden. The same idea applies to code: each part exposes a small public surface and hides its internals.
A. What the user sees (progressive disclosure)
Every screen follows three levels.
Level
Shows
Example
0, glance
One headline number, one insight, one primary action
Home: net balance this month, one insight line, an "Add" button
1, one tap
The detail behind the headline
