API
Why wait
Account Aggregator (AA) through a licensed gateway such as Setu, Finvu or OneMoney
Gives automatic bank data with user consent, but AA users are institutions called FIUs that must follow ReBIT API specifications and sandbox onboarding (Sahamati). Confirm that a personal-finance app can qualify, or can go through a technology provider, before promising it.
A licensed payment aggregator (Razorpay, Cashfree, PayU)
Only needed if you want bank-verified settlement. It requires a business account, KYC and signed webhooks.
Play Console SMS exception for money management
Google lists SMS-based money management as a possible use, but it is subject to Play review and approval (Google Play policy). Apply only if auto-capture proves essential.
Never use
• Screen-scraping or asking for bank passwords.
• READ_SMS, READ_CALL_LOG, or an accessibility service to read other apps.
• Gemini or any API key inside the APK.
• UPI Collect or typed-VPA payment screens as the main flow.
• Room, or any second financial database.
AI model rule
Do not hard-code gemini-2.5-flash. Google's deprecation page lists it with a shutdown date (Gemini API deprecations), and developer reports say 2.5 models returned errors earlier than announced and were later limited to accounts that had used them before (Google AI developer forum). Instead:
1. Open the current Firebase AI Logic model list (Firebase docs) and choose a currently supported stable Flash-tier model.
2. Store the model id in Remote Config, with the chosen id as the in-app default.
3. Add one fallback model id, and fall back automatically on a "model not found" error.
