8. Roommate ledger and UPI settlement
Split modes
EQUAL, EXACT, PERCENTAGE and SHARES. EQUAL is the default; the other three sit behind "More split options". All allocation is in paise and must sum exactly to the expense.
• EQUAL: base share = total divided by participants; the leftover paise go one each to the first participants in a fixed order (sorted by uid).
• EXACT: the entered amounts must sum to the total, or the form shows how much is left.
• PERCENTAGE: percentages are held in basis points and must sum to 10,000. Use the largest-remainder method for rounding, with a uid tie-break.
• SHARES: positive integer weights, allocated by the same largest-remainder method.
Validate: participants are household members, no duplicates, positive shares, valid percentages, and the payer is a participant or is explicitly marked as paying for others. Show four different numbers, never blended: amount owed, amount paid, outstanding balance and settled amount. An optional "simplify debts" view sits at Level 2.
