UPI settlement handoff
PaymentManager builds a standard personal-payment intent: upi://pay?pa=<VPA>&pn=<name>&am=<amount, 2 decimals>&cu=INR&tn=<note>. It is for person-to-person settlement only. Merchant or collection flows need a licensed payment aggregator and are out of scope.
Why no typed VPAs in the main path: NPCI guidance effective February 2026 restricts manual VPA entry on mobile and makes intent the standard flow (Razorpay on NPCI guidelines). So the user confirms a saved payee once (VPA validated by pattern and shown masked), and later settlements need one tap. Offer QR scan as an alternative way to add a payee.
• Validate the VPA pattern and the amount (positive, at most 2 decimals, within MAX_AMOUNT_MINOR). Do not hard-code bank transaction limits.
• Use the Android app chooser. If no UPI app exists, say so and offer "Copy VPA".
• Handle cancel and failure results. Treat any result data from the UPI app as a hint only, because it can be missing or forged.
